{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"28398591a8b1f7a1","name":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/OceaniaStorm/units/card_unit_2nd_west_africa","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"2nd WEST AFRICA","text":"Deployment: Draw the cheapest order from your deck. Repeat if it did not start there.","flavorText":"The 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade was a British Army formation made up of battalions of the Royal West African Frontier Force. Originally formed as the 4th (Gold Coast) Infantry Brigade, it fought in the East African Campaign, advancing from Kenya into Italian Somaliland and Ethiopia as part of the 2nd (African) Division. After returning to West Africa in late 1941, the formation was reorganized and renamed the 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade. In 1944, it joined the 82nd (West Africa) Division and was deployed to Burma. During the Third Arakan Campaign, the brigade advanced through the Kalapanzin Valley and crossed difficult, jungle-covered mountain terrain toward Myohaung. Its advance, together with other West African forces, helped force the Japanese to abandon the Mayu Peninsula. The brigade continued pressing south along the coast and captured the port of Gwa shortly before Japanese forces withdrew from Burma.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa_title","SourceString":"2nd WEST AFRICA","LocalizedString":"2nd WEST AFRICA"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa_text","SourceString":"Deployment: Draw the cheapest order from your deck. Repeat if it did not start there.","LocalizedString":"Deployment: Draw the cheapest order from your deck. Repeat if it did not start there."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa_history","SourceString":"The 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade was a British Army formation made up of battalions of the Royal West African Frontier Force. Originally formed as the 4th (Gold Coast) Infantry Brigade, it fought in the East African Campaign, advancing from Kenya into Italian Somaliland and Ethiopia as part of the 2nd (African) Division. After returning to West Africa in late 1941, the formation was reorganized and renamed the 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade. In 1944, it joined the 82nd (West Africa) Division and was deployed to Burma. During the Third Arakan Campaign, the brigade advanced through the Kalapanzin Valley and crossed difficult, jungle-covered mountain terrain toward Myohaung. Its advance, together with other West African forces, helped force the Japanese to abandon the Mayu Peninsula. The brigade continued pressing south along the coast and captured the port of Gwa shortly before Japanese forces withdrew from Burma.","LocalizedString":"The 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade was a British Army formation made up of battalions of the Royal West African Frontier Force. Originally formed as the 4th (Gold Coast) Infantry Brigade, it fought in the East African Campaign, advancing from Kenya into Italian Somaliland and Ethiopia as part of the 2nd (African) Division. After returning to West Africa in late 1941, the formation was reorganized and renamed the 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade. In 1944, it joined the 82nd (West Africa) Division and was deployed to Burma. During the Third Arakan Campaign, the brigade advanced through the Kalapanzin Valley and crossed difficult, jungle-covered mountain terrain toward Myohaung. Its advance, together with other West African forces, helped force the Japanese to abandon the Mayu Peninsula. The brigade continued pressing south along the coast and captured the port of Gwa shortly before Japanese forces withdrew from Burma."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::OceaniaStorm","hasDeployment":true,"historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/2nd_WEST_AFRICA.2nd_WEST_AFRICA","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":450.0,"Y":512.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa_photo","SourceString":"A Polish officer and a mortar team of the 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade. Third Arakan Campaign, Burma, 1945.","LocalizedString":"A Polish officer and a mortar team of the 2nd (West Africa) Infantry Brigade. Third Arakan Campaign, Burma, 1945."},"historyTypeDescription":{"Namespace":"","Key":"0DBC5F184A8F0CFAA1A9D6BB449E2AC6","SourceString":"Infantry","LocalizedString":"Infantry"},"blowUpExplosionNiagara":{"ObjectName":"NiagaraSystem'NS_ExplosionInfantryS'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Effects/Niagara/NS_ExplosionInfantryS.46"},"blowUpCameraShake":{"ObjectName":"BlueprintGeneratedClass'CameraShakeLight_C'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/examples/GrenadePack/Blueprints/CameraShakeLight.0"},"OnAttackVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/Infantry/BP_AttackInfantry.BP_AttackInfantry_C","SubPathString":""}},"variables":[{"name":"PossibleCards","type":"TArray<UBaseCardObject*>","direction":"in"},{"name":"cardDeveloped","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"objSet","type":"bool","direction":"in"},{"name":"cheapeastCard","type":"UBaseCardObject*","direction":"in"},{"name":"myDeck","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"}],"functions":[{"name":"ExecuteUbergraph_card_unit_2nd_west_africa","owner":"card_unit_2nd_west_africa_C","params":[{"name":"EntryPoint","type":"int32","direction":"in"}],"pure":false,"event":false,"flags":"FUNC_Final | FUNC_UbergraphFunction | FUNC_HasDefaults","locals":[{"name":"Temp_int_Loop_Counter_Variable","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"CallFunc_Add_IntInt_ReturnValue","type":"int32","direction":"in"},{"name":"Temp_int_Array_Index_Var